  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Et</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Et vindicandi semet, per du-</l>
    <l n="2">ella periculosa &amp; impia, inno-</l>
    <l n="3">centibus ablata foret occasio.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Neque enim de duellis, in-</l>
    <l n="5">juriati cogitarent, certo per-</l>
    <l n="6">suasi, per publicas personas</l>
    <l n="7">vindictam sibi fore paratam.</l>
    <l n="8">Nec contumelias pro ludo &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">joco haberent maledici, si</l>
    <l n="10">scirent, se non impune, hoc</l>
    <l n="11">esse laturos. Ita Imperator</l>
    <l n="12">Marcus, quo à vitiis deterreret</l>
    <l n="13">saevientem nimium, hoc suo</l>
    <l n="14">inseruit edicto, <i>sciat me hoc ad-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>missum severius executurum.</i> Ac si</l>
    <l n="16">non major effet deterrendi ratio,</l>
    <l n="17">quam rigida poenarum adver-</l>
    <l n="18">sus injuriantem executio. Quę</l>
    <l n="19">etiam ratio fuit, quod antiqui</l>
    <l n="20">legislatores multum curarent,</l>
    <l n="21">ne cui impunita foret menti-</l>
    <l n="22">endi libido. Hinc calumnian-</l>
    <l n="23">tes ad vindictam poscebat ex</l>
    <l n="24">l. Rhemmia similitudo, sup-</l>
    <l n="25">plicii, ex aliis legibus, aliae</l>
    <l n="26">poenae statutae, &amp; quidem satis</l>
    <l n="27">graves.</l>
  </main_text>
